=================== G4
public atom H(term t)
H(string s) -> :s
H(_) -> :other
--- prototype 2:
G4/m.bs:4:3: error: `string` cannot name a pattern
  `is_binary` is true of more values than `string` holds,
  so one test does not decide it: it can be declared, passed and
  returned, and never matched on. Matching one is not built.
  The refusal is temporary by construction — the day a pattern form
  reaches inside, the type becomes decidable and it lifts.
  A type prefix names a record, whose minted tag the pattern matches,
  or a part the platform tests whole: `int`, `float`, `atom`,
=================== G5
type Meters = int where value >= 0
public atom H(int | :none t)
H(Meters m) -> :m
H(int i) -> :neg
H(:none) -> :none
